## 7. EXECUTION MODE: SCALP

### 7.1 Definition

Trade short-term oscillations around VWAP/POC in a balanced, liquid market.

> "if you're someone who does very dynamic scalping, then the VWAP can be very sideways oriented. And from the opening trade variant, the market should also be more sideways weighted, for example, non-trend or something like that. Then you have the opportunity to keep looking for shorts at the top and keep looking for longs at the bottom until a reversal of the market environment eventually occurs."
> **Source GPS:** 43JaKHRvxHk | [END]

### 7.2 When Valid

**A. ONLY When VWAP Is Sideways**

> "in a sequence like this, you mustn't trade a trend continuation. You absolutely have to go for counter trades. And that's the most crucial thing if you want to use the VWAP as a scalper, that you go ahead and say, 'Only if the VWAP is currently oriented sideways, and I can't assume a maximally brutal breakout now or a trend day from the market open, then I can use this whole model for myself.'"
> **Source GPS:** 43JaKHRvxHk | [MIDDLE]

**Tier:** T5 — Tom's command.

### 7.3 Zone Requirements

- VWAP/POC as equilibrium
- Price ranges around VWAP

> "You can define so-called price ranges from the VWAP where you expect a reaction."
> **Source GPS:** 43JaKHRvxHk | [MIDDLE]

### 7.4 Proof Requirements

**A. No Breakout Assumption**

> "I can't assume a maximally brutal breakout now or a trend day from the market open"
> **Source GPS:** 43JaKHRvxHk | [MIDDLE]

### 7.5 R:R Reality

> "if you need verifiable numbers, then you need And if I were to only ever take the trade up to the VWAP, I can already see those are very modest profit targets. And where do I have to set my stop loss? So, where do I give up on my trade? And there you already see the risk-reward ratio for such, let's call them, intraday scalpers. Intraday? Yes, they're scalpers cutting out small sequences in terms of the risk-reward ratio. It's very modest"
> **Source GPS:** 43JaKHRvxHk | [MIDDLE]

**Tier:** T1 — Tom's example.

### 7.6 Scalper vs Swing Trader Distinction

> "for the scalpers, they're getting out up here now. But we intraday swing traders, breakout traders who are waiting for the explosion. We wait"
> **Source GPS:** 4MoNjEQ2Dd8 | [MIDDLE]

